  "tagline": "Low-maintenance embeddable RDBMS with built-in TimeSeries, still quietly running retail and telco systems.",
  "description": "Informix is a relational database known for running for years with almost no DBA attention, which made it popular for embedding in retail point-of-sale, telecom and utility systems. Its distinctive pieces are a native TimeSeries storage type that is very compact for meter and sensor data, MACH 11 high-availability clusters, Enterprise Replication for multi-site active-active, and a wire listener that speaks the MongoDB protocol. IBM still owns it and co-develops it with HCLSoftware; version 15 lifted many old size limits and fix packs ship regularly (15.0.1.18 in September 2026). It is a solid choice for existing estates but has a small community for new projects.",
